{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.083,
            0.573,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": "The separated grains get mixed with piles of husk."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.125,
            0.57,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": "Valli whispers to Malli, “Will the farmers handpick the grains to remove them from so much husk?” She wonders, “How much time will the farmers take to separate these?”"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.616,
            0.089,
            0.833,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": "A small amount of puffed rice is mixed with chana dal. Can you think of separating the mixture by any method other than handpicking?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.229,
            0.566,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "Let us perform an activity to find out the answer to the questions raised by Valli."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.283,
            0.406,
            0.305
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 9.1: Let us explore"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.315,
            0.742,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": " Take a handful of roasted peanuts and rub them between your palms. What happens?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.361,
            0.742,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": "Is it possible to separate the removed skin and the peanuts?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.406,
            0.614,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": " Now, try blowing it. What do you observe?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.43,
            0.742,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": "Which of these components—removed peanut skins or peanuts are blown away?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.473,
            0.742,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "You observe that blowing air separates the heavier and the lighter components."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.514,
            0.743,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "How do you think farmers separate so many grains from husk?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.555,
            0.743,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": "Traditionally, a soop (bamboo tray) is used for separating heavier and lighter components of a mixture (Fig. 9.3)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.598,
            0.426,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "Next day, their Nana takes them to the fields to show this process at work."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.66,
            0.426,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "Malli and Valli observe a farmer standing on a raised platform. The farmer is moving the bamboo tray which contains threshed wheat grains in the direction of air or wind (Fig. 9.4)."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.441,
            0.601,
            0.809,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.528,
                0.753,
                0.702,
                0.77
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 9.3: Bamboo tray"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.805,
            0.744,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": "What do you **infer** from Fig. 9.4? Do both the components, wheat grains and husk, fall at the same place? Which of the two components get blown away? Can the wind separate the two components?"
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
            0.874,
            0.755,
            0.913,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": "in Everyday Life Methods of Separation"
        },
        {
